  1301→### Expected Emergent Behaviors
  1302→
  1303→- **Training Arms Race**: Competitive pressure drives continuous training
  1304→- **Boom-Bust Cycles**: Training spikes followed by inference-heavy periods
  1305→- **Strategic Timing**: Train when competitors are weak, run when you're ahead
  1306→- **Scale Economics**: Larger orgs can afford bigger, riskier training runs
  1307→- **Model Generations**: Discrete jumps in capability as new models deploy
  1308→- **Compute Scarcity**: Training competes with research, creates bottlenecks
  1309→
  1310→This enhancement will make the compute allocation problem **truly strategic** rather than just a fixed percentage split.
